A||N||2||Ozzy||Drive Axle seals...||||1||
Z||000000||Ozzy||05-15-2000||12:15 AM||||Hi folks.<P>Can anyone tell me if they have replaced the driveaxle seals on a Isuzu 5 spd in an '88 model with the engine/tanny still in the vehicle? I hear they are a tight fit need assistance of a tool of some sort to press them in square.<P>I have a leak on the left axle (drivers side). Is this the only seal required to hold transmission fluid?<P>TIA<P>Ozzy||||reg||1
Z||000001||batboy||05-15-2000||12:50 AM||||Yes, the axle seals can be replace with the tranny in the car. The "tool" I used was a piece of PVC pipe. The Fiero On-line Service Guide describes the diameter etc.<P>There is another "front" seal in the tranny too, but you have to drop the cradle to get to that one. It's between the tranny and engine.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Ozzy||05-15-2000||07:25 PM||||Thnx Batboy...Never any "<I>Bat guanno</I>" outta you!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>I'm certain that this leak is coming from the driveaxle area.<P>I have read the article you mentioned too. I don't think it described the procedure as an in place deal...maybe I need to read it again!<P>Ozzy<p>[This message has been edited by Ozzy (edited 05-15-2000).]||||reg||1
